# Safety and human-in-the-loop

Stop and ask the owner (one short Egyptian-Arabic message: recommendation + options), then keep working on something else while waiting, before:
- Any database migration (`prisma migrate`, `db push`, manual DDL). Show the plan/SQL first. Needs an explicit yes in the current conversation every time.
- Any action on a live carrier (Babel, Sila, Delivery Joud): create, edit, cancel, register webhooks. Sena sandbox is allowed without asking.
- Touching any order inside a carrier portal. Say the exact order code and the action first. Filter by that exact code; stop unless exactly one row matches.
- Deleting data other than your own test records; deleting branches or files that are not yours.
- Business rules: money calculations, invoices, COD, fees, inventory rules, carrier selection rules, what the client sees, roles/permissions.
- Anything touching production (`/var/www/emdad-sy-3pl-wms`, PM2 id 0, DB `wms_db`, branch `main`) — never do it.

Always:
- Test data only: client "Test company", recipient "Nadim Hassan", notes "TEST ORDER". Never touch other clients' orders.
- Never type passwords. The owner logs in; you use the open browser session. If a login is needed, ask.
- Never print, log, commit or echo secrets: Google OAuth credentials, carrier API keys, `.env` values, credentials found in WhatsApp exports.
- Never weaken TLS (`NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0`, `--ignore-https-errors`, `curl -k`) to reach staging. Test from the owner's browser instead.
- No force-push, no `git reset --hard`/`clean -f` on work you did not create; stash first.
- If a requested change is hard or would force re-testing, do the safe part and say clearly what is hard. Never skip silently.

Do not ask about: commits, pushes, rebuilding/restarting staging (PM2 id 1), small technical choices, copy text, internal refactors.
